WEBVTT

00:00:11.990 --> 00:00:15.680
Lenny-chan, happy birthday!

00:00:17.380 --> 00:00:20.980
Thank you so much everyone! Thank you!

00:00:20.980 --> 00:00:22.120
Here, this is for you.

00:00:23.320 --> 00:00:26.750
It's a birthday present 
from us, the Crimson Vow.

00:00:27.280 --> 00:00:29.350
Thank you! This makes me so happy!

00:00:30.370 --> 00:00:32.700
I wonder what it could be. 
I wonder what it could be!

00:00:36.030 --> 00:00:40.100
I tried to express your cuteness 
just as it is, Lenny-chan.

00:00:40.100 --> 00:00:44.270
Only you could do this, Mile. Your carving 
skills are as amazing as ever.

00:00:44.270 --> 00:00:45.340
But...

00:00:46.040 --> 00:00:49.280
This one area seems to have 
been slightly exaggerated.

00:00:49.280 --> 00:00:50.150
That's...!

00:00:50.390 --> 00:00:52.530
It's not like I'm envious or jealous,

00:00:52.530 --> 00:00:55.530
or wishing I was that type, too...

00:00:55.530 --> 00:00:57.780
I'm not thinking any of that at all!

00:01:04.560 --> 00:01:09.320
Lenny-chan, it seems like you've gotten used 
to your role as the face of this inn.

00:01:09.320 --> 00:01:13.420
Us old guys'll keep being your fans, 
so keep up the good work, okay?

00:01:13.420 --> 00:01:15.380
Thank you!

00:01:15.720 --> 00:01:18.520
That Lenny... She looks like she's having fun.

00:01:18.520 --> 00:01:21.640
Birthdays really are fun, aren't they?

00:01:21.640 --> 00:01:26.550
Oh... Now I've started remembering what 
it was like back at the academy.

00:01:26.550 --> 00:01:28.020
The Academy?

00:01:28.190 --> 00:01:31.150
You mean the Eckland Academy 
you mentioned before?

00:01:31.720 --> 00:01:32.460
Yes.

00:03:01.860 --> 00:03:03.990
Didn't I Say to Make My Abilities 
Average in the Next Life?!

00:03:04.760 --> 00:03:09.000
<b>Episode 10</b>

00:03:04.760 --> 00:03:09.000
<b>Didn't I Say Surprises Should Be Kept Secret?!</b>

00:03:16.580 --> 00:03:17.880
It's amazing!

00:03:18.300 --> 00:03:22.100
I'm so sorry you went to all this 
trouble just to celebrate my birthday.

00:03:22.100 --> 00:03:24.160
Of course we'd do this, Adele-san.

00:03:24.160 --> 00:03:27.760
We borrowed the dormitory 
kitchen to make all of this.

00:03:27.760 --> 00:03:29.660
I hope it tastes good.

00:03:31.570 --> 00:03:34.520
Marcela-sama was so excited about everything!

00:03:34.520 --> 00:03:35.390
Yes, she was!

00:03:35.390 --> 00:03:37.840
What? Monika-san! Aureana-san!

00:03:37.840 --> 00:03:41.630
I w-wouldn't say I was especially 
excited or anything.

00:03:49.160 --> 00:03:50.950
What's wrong, Adele-chan?

00:03:50.950 --> 00:03:52.550
Are you laughing?

00:03:52.960 --> 00:03:55.960
Did we say something amusing?

00:03:56.190 --> 00:03:59.480
I'm not laughing! I'm so moved, I'm crying!

00:03:59.480 --> 00:04:02.560
I mean... This is the first time for me.

00:04:02.980 --> 00:04:06.900
Having friends who would celebrate 
my birthday with me is just...

00:04:10.900 --> 00:04:14.400
Oh, Adele... You shouldn't 
cry over something like this.

00:04:14.400 --> 00:04:17.610
That's right. Of course 
we'd celebrate with you.

00:04:17.870 --> 00:04:21.360
After all, we are friends.

00:04:21.940 --> 00:04:23.020
Everyone...

00:04:26.890 --> 00:04:29.540
Happy birthday, Adele-san!

00:04:29.540 --> 00:04:30.650
Thank you!

00:04:33.040 --> 00:04:35.500
...is how it happened.

00:04:35.780 --> 00:04:37.700
We all ate cake together.

00:04:37.700 --> 00:04:38.290
Oh!

00:04:38.290 --> 00:04:42.620
That Marcela-san put whipped 
cream on the end of her nose!

00:04:42.620 --> 00:04:44.950
We just couldn't stop laughing!

00:04:47.160 --> 00:04:49.100
Really. Is that so.

00:04:49.380 --> 00:04:53.120
It really was such a fun birthday.

00:04:53.580 --> 00:04:56.100
I wonder if everyone's doing okay.

00:04:58.110 --> 00:05:00.110
<b>Baths</b>

00:04:58.780 --> 00:05:00.110
I don't like it.

00:05:01.150 --> 00:05:03.620
What do you mean, "cream 
on the end of her nose"?

00:05:03.620 --> 00:05:06.020
What do you mean, "we couldn't stop laughing"?

00:05:06.020 --> 00:05:07.820
And getting all giddy over it like that...

00:05:07.820 --> 00:05:09.330
That Mile!

00:05:10.960 --> 00:05:13.660
I can't eat any more...

00:05:14.510 --> 00:05:16.080
Oh, Reina. Are you jealous?

00:05:16.320 --> 00:05:18.280
N-No, I'm not!

00:05:18.280 --> 00:05:19.530
Whatever happened in the past,

00:05:19.530 --> 00:05:23.530
Mile is officially one of us now!
Part of the Crimson Vow!

00:05:23.530 --> 00:05:26.090
I'm not getting beat by some 
friends in her memories.

00:05:26.410 --> 00:05:29.470
Th-This is just a sense of rivalry! Rivalry!

00:05:29.870 --> 00:05:32.970
Society does tend to call 
that "jealousy," though.

00:05:33.220 --> 00:05:34.770
Oh, honestly!

00:05:34.770 --> 00:05:38.020
Why isn't today Mile's birthday?

00:05:38.020 --> 00:05:41.980
If it were, then we could've given 
her a party that was just as fun!

00:05:42.240 --> 00:05:44.400
Today is Lenny-chan's birthday, right?

00:05:44.400 --> 00:05:46.020
You don't ask for much, do you?

00:05:46.020 --> 00:05:48.510
I guess, though, even if 
it's not her birthday,

00:05:48.510 --> 00:05:52.170
if it were some kind of anniversary, 
we could celebrate that, but...

00:05:55.200 --> 00:05:57.210
It <i>is</i> an anniversary!

00:05:57.210 --> 00:05:57.960
Huh?

00:05:58.610 --> 00:06:04.210
It's been nearly two hundred days since 
we met Mile at the Hunter Prep School!

00:06:05.710 --> 00:06:06.670
That's it!

00:06:08.180 --> 00:06:09.180
What?

00:06:09.670 --> 00:06:12.130
You're going to celebrate the 
anniversary of two hundred days

00:06:12.130 --> 00:06:14.180
since we met at the Hunter 
Prep School with me?

00:06:14.430 --> 00:06:18.310
Of course we will, Mile. 
It's your anniversary, after all.

00:06:20.520 --> 00:06:22.510
This is the best, Reina-san!

00:06:22.510 --> 00:06:26.030
I'm so glad I joined the Crimson Vow!

00:06:30.770 --> 00:06:34.540
This'll work! It'll make Mile 
super happy! I'm sure of it!

00:06:36.800 --> 00:06:39.370
She seems to be getting 
excited all on her own over there.

00:06:39.740 --> 00:06:41.670
But Reina's right.

00:06:41.670 --> 00:06:45.050
I'm sure that if we do this for her, 
it will make Mile-chan very happy.

00:06:45.260 --> 00:06:46.760
Yes, I suppose that's true.

00:06:49.060 --> 00:06:51.050
Now it's decided!
It's time to make it happen!

00:06:51.050 --> 00:06:52.000
Yeah!

00:06:58.540 --> 00:07:01.650
Let's see, let's see... 
What kind of work is there today?

00:07:01.930 --> 00:07:04.570
What about this one? Hmm...

00:07:04.940 --> 00:07:08.850
This one is... not so great.

00:07:08.850 --> 00:07:11.160
Are there any quests that stand out?

00:07:11.600 --> 00:07:14.410
Which one should we make our next job, guys?

00:07:15.430 --> 00:07:18.750
Oh! Sorry, I have something 
I need to do, so...

00:07:18.970 --> 00:07:22.040
That's right. I have some minor 
things to take care of today.

00:07:22.220 --> 00:07:26.360
And I... I haven't done thorough 
maintenance on my sword in a long time,

00:07:26.360 --> 00:07:27.510
so I have to do that.

00:07:27.510 --> 00:07:28.170
Yup!

00:07:32.680 --> 00:07:34.300
Guys?

00:07:35.930 --> 00:07:37.720
Fireball!

00:07:39.480 --> 00:07:41.350
Wind Storm!

00:07:43.640 --> 00:07:46.350
Godspeed sword! 1.3x speed!

00:07:49.730 --> 00:07:51.320
That was a little tougher than usual.

00:07:51.720 --> 00:07:54.850
If Mile were here, a rock lizard
 would be an easy catch.

00:07:54.850 --> 00:07:56.280
What are you talking about?

00:07:56.280 --> 00:07:58.950
If we don't earn the money ourselves, 
there's no point, right?

00:07:59.520 --> 00:08:01.450
Celebrations mean presents!

00:08:01.450 --> 00:08:05.260
That's why we've thoroughly investigated 
exactly what Mile wants!

00:08:06.840 --> 00:08:10.760
Oh, I like that! It's so pretty!

00:08:11.010 --> 00:08:13.260
I wish I could have it!

00:08:19.810 --> 00:08:24.410
But for her to want an expensive 
accessory like that, of all things...

00:08:24.410 --> 00:08:26.610
It's way over budget.

00:08:26.970 --> 00:08:30.600
It just means Mile's like 
any other girl that way.

00:08:30.600 --> 00:08:32.740
Though she isn't normal in any other way.

00:08:33.240 --> 00:08:35.450
Okay! On to the next quest!

00:08:35.680 --> 00:08:39.450
We're gonna earn a ton and surprise Mile!

00:08:39.450 --> 00:08:41.700
<b>The Next Day</b>

00:08:41.930 --> 00:08:44.120
Um, Reina-san, about work today...

00:08:44.390 --> 00:08:46.590
Sorry, I've got other plans today, too.

00:08:46.590 --> 00:08:47.540
Huh?

00:08:47.940 --> 00:08:48.920
Pauline-san!

00:08:48.920 --> 00:08:51.420
I'm sorry, Mile-chan. I've got something, too.

00:08:53.340 --> 00:08:56.270
Oh, right! I have to do some 
maintenance on my sword!

00:08:56.270 --> 00:08:59.350
Mavis-san! You just did maintenance 
on your sword yesterday!

00:08:59.350 --> 00:09:01.560
Oh! Busy, busy!

00:09:04.030 --> 00:09:05.310
Very suspicious...

00:09:05.540 --> 00:09:08.430
Honestly! Sudden business! 
Minor matters! Sword maintenance!

00:09:08.430 --> 00:09:11.160
Lately, everyone's been going off somewhere!

00:09:11.160 --> 00:09:12.390
Do they not need me anymore?

00:09:12.390 --> 00:09:13.360
Are they leaving me out?

00:09:13.360 --> 00:09:15.650
Am I going back to being all alone?

00:09:16.060 --> 00:09:19.590
If it bothers you so much,
why don't you look into what they're doing?

00:09:19.590 --> 00:09:21.410
You can use that detection 
magic you excel at.

00:09:21.610 --> 00:09:22.690
Oh, right!

00:09:23.140 --> 00:09:25.540
For Mile's Devil Ears hear all!

00:09:25.540 --> 00:09:26.550
But...

00:09:26.550 --> 00:09:29.680
I can't do that. It'd be 
a violation of privacy.

00:09:29.680 --> 00:09:32.170
You do seem to be very honest 
in these sorts of situations.

00:09:32.530 --> 00:09:35.300
You don't have any idea at 
all what might be going on?

00:09:35.540 --> 00:09:38.200
A reason they might be leaving you out.

00:09:38.200 --> 00:09:39.960
How would I have any idea wha—

00:09:40.920 --> 00:09:42.280
Could it be...

00:10:01.410 --> 00:10:02.760
Yummy!

00:10:02.760 --> 00:10:06.620
Pauline-san found out I've been 
snacking on the sweets she hid?

00:10:12.500 --> 00:10:13.400
Okay!

00:10:14.420 --> 00:10:17.300
Whoops! Little too soon
to wake up there, baby.

00:10:18.670 --> 00:10:20.340
No one's won this contest yet!

00:10:20.340 --> 00:10:22.840
Or maybe Reina-san's realized I've 
been measuring her chest

00:10:22.840 --> 00:10:25.700
while she's sleeping, then feeling relieved?

00:10:35.710 --> 00:10:37.730
Her art is the best!

00:10:37.730 --> 00:10:41.320
It couldn't be that Mavis-san knows I've 
been secretly reading her picture diary?

00:10:41.320 --> 00:10:44.370
You're guilty of quite a bit,
 aren't you, Mile-sama?

00:10:44.600 --> 00:10:47.550
What do I do? At this rate, I'll...

00:10:50.630 --> 00:10:51.540
Don't hit the face.

00:10:51.890 --> 00:10:53.400
Go for the body.

00:10:53.400 --> 00:10:55.120
Gotcha, boss.

00:10:55.120 --> 00:10:58.260
Hey! Whaddaya think you're lookin' at?
 You think you're better than us?

00:10:58.630 --> 00:11:01.440
Wh-What have I done?

00:11:01.440 --> 00:11:04.140
I haven't done anything to make you angry...

00:11:04.400 --> 00:11:07.500
Oh! I just need to jump, right? I'll jump.

00:11:10.620 --> 00:11:13.060
You see? I don't have any money.

00:11:14.420 --> 00:11:16.440
We've never liked you.

00:11:16.680 --> 00:11:19.320
Going around, acting like an honors student...
Who d'you think you are?

00:11:19.940 --> 00:11:23.490
Don't go getting cocky just 'cuz you're 
the only one who's got a previous life!

00:11:23.490 --> 00:11:24.740
Don't get cocky!

00:11:24.740 --> 00:11:25.650
Let's go.

00:11:29.740 --> 00:11:32.250
Why is this happening to me?

00:11:32.480 --> 00:11:36.590
O God! I can't see your face for the tears!

00:11:38.680 --> 00:11:40.440
What a handful.

00:11:40.440 --> 00:11:43.970
Then why don't you just 
go and ask them directly?

00:11:49.210 --> 00:11:51.440
<i>How am I supposed to ask them anything?</i>

00:11:51.440 --> 00:11:56.190
<i>I can't just say, "Hey guys! 
Why are you leaving me out?"</i>

00:11:56.520 --> 00:11:58.940
<i>What is this strange sense of tension?</i>

00:11:59.960 --> 00:12:02.320
<i>This is why I'm no good with secrets.</i>

00:12:02.680 --> 00:12:04.840
<i>We just need to hang in there until next week.</i>

00:12:04.840 --> 00:12:07.830
<i>We have to stay strong until we 
have enough money for her present!</i>

00:12:09.150 --> 00:12:10.290
U-Um!

00:12:14.290 --> 00:12:17.870
Uh... The weather was nice today, wasn't it?

00:12:18.400 --> 00:12:21.510
Y-Yes, it was. Very nice weather.

00:12:27.280 --> 00:12:29.260
Thank you for your patronage!

00:12:29.640 --> 00:12:31.450
Hope you come to see us again soon!

00:12:33.080 --> 00:12:34.640
Hey! Hey, Lenny-chan!

00:12:34.640 --> 00:12:38.020
Have Reina-san or the others 
said anything about me?

00:12:38.260 --> 00:12:42.150
Reina-san or the others? About you, Mile-san?

00:12:42.150 --> 00:12:43.160
Yes!

00:12:43.160 --> 00:12:46.410
If you tell me, I promise 
I won't say anything, Lenny-chan.

00:12:46.660 --> 00:12:50.120
Complaints, insults, 
or anything else! Just tell me!

00:12:50.120 --> 00:12:50.660
Please?

00:12:50.960 --> 00:12:52.940
Complaints?

00:12:52.940 --> 00:12:54.570
I haven't heard anything...

00:12:55.610 --> 00:12:57.390
<i>What should I do?</i>

00:12:57.390 --> 00:13:02.670
<i>They made me swear not to say anything, 
no matter what Mile-san asked.</i>

00:13:02.910 --> 00:13:05.520
Oh! Do you not want to say 
because you feel bad for me?

00:13:05.520 --> 00:13:07.170
Don't worry! I'm fine!

00:13:07.170 --> 00:13:09.960
Despite how I look, 
I'm pretty strong emotionally.

00:13:09.960 --> 00:13:13.020
<i>That's a lie. She doesn't 
seem like that type at all!</i>

00:13:14.480 --> 00:13:16.270
Bring it on!

00:13:16.270 --> 00:13:17.940
What are you saying?

00:13:17.940 --> 00:13:23.530
I wouldn't hide things from you, would I?

00:13:23.720 --> 00:13:26.090
Well... I'll just be going now.

00:13:26.530 --> 00:13:30.280
Lenny-chan, we've been friends since before 
I went to the Hunter School, right?

00:13:30.280 --> 00:13:34.470
And I was the one who said we should 
make this our base after graduation.

00:13:34.470 --> 00:13:37.760
I was the one who taught everyone how 
to behave while working in a maid café.

00:13:37.760 --> 00:13:38.710
And the baths!

00:13:38.710 --> 00:13:40.870
We could have just moved to a different inn,

00:13:40.870 --> 00:13:43.090
but I convinced everyone 
that we should build baths

00:13:43.090 --> 00:13:46.170
at this inn with our earnings 
from working as the Crimson Vow!

00:13:46.170 --> 00:13:48.430
Pauline-san is so opinionated about money.

00:13:48.430 --> 00:13:50.300
Do you have any idea how hard that was?

00:13:50.300 --> 00:13:51.540
No!

00:13:51.540 --> 00:13:54.310
I'm sorry! I'm busy with work!

00:13:55.330 --> 00:13:56.860
Even Lenny-chan is...

00:13:56.860 --> 00:14:00.020
Mile-sama, what on earth are you doing?

00:14:00.020 --> 00:14:01.820
Oh! Could it be...

00:14:03.020 --> 00:14:10.030
<b>Crimson Vow</b>

00:14:03.020 --> 00:14:10.030
<b>New Member Announcement</b>

00:14:03.310 --> 00:14:06.280
I'm the Crimson Vow's new member, Lenny!

00:14:06.280 --> 00:14:10.030
I'm still a novice Hunter, 
but I hope for your support!

00:14:13.070 --> 00:14:16.630
There you have it. Thank you for 
your service thus far, Mile-chan.

00:14:16.630 --> 00:14:17.410
What?

00:14:17.410 --> 00:14:18.520
Congratulations.

00:14:18.520 --> 00:14:21.040
Starting today, you're an average girl,
 just like you always wanted.

00:14:22.560 --> 00:14:26.780
W-Wait! Why am I suddenly 
graduating from the group?

00:14:26.780 --> 00:14:29.630
Even adding Lenny-chan, couldn't we
 just work as a group of five?

00:14:30.020 --> 00:14:31.300
Isn't it obvious?

00:14:31.590 --> 00:14:35.850
We don't need two flat-chested 
characters on the same team!

00:14:35.560 --> 00:14:36.930
<b>Only</b>

00:14:35.560 --> 00:14:36.930
<b>One</b>

00:14:36.930 --> 00:14:41.550
We don't need two flat-chested characters!

00:14:45.900 --> 00:14:47.010
It's over.

00:14:47.440 --> 00:14:50.040
Everything's gone white...

00:14:50.560 --> 00:14:53.890
Burned through with nothing left...
but white ash.

00:14:54.330 --> 00:14:56.600
Old man... Hey, old man...

00:14:56.600 --> 00:14:58.000
Who are you calling "old man"?

00:14:58.000 --> 00:15:00.400
Help me get my gloves off...

00:15:00.400 --> 00:15:02.400
You're not wearing any.

00:15:02.400 --> 00:15:03.780
Is Youko here?

00:15:03.780 --> 00:15:08.390
I want you to take these guys... 
I want you to have them.

00:15:08.390 --> 00:15:10.040
Who are you talking to?

00:15:16.710 --> 00:15:21.440
Once we obtain this cockatrice, 
our mission will finally be complete.

00:15:21.440 --> 00:15:23.860
We managed to make it in time for today.

00:15:24.310 --> 00:15:25.860
And as for the accessory we were eyeing...

00:15:25.860 --> 00:15:28.320
After we clear this quest, 
we should be able to buy it.

00:15:29.310 --> 00:15:33.360
I wonder what Mile's face will look 
like when we throw her a celebration.

00:15:33.360 --> 00:15:36.410
You think she'll be so moved she starts crying?

00:15:41.240 --> 00:15:42.370
Hmph...

00:15:42.370 --> 00:15:43.300
Fine, then.

00:15:43.300 --> 00:15:46.000
If they're going to ignore me, 
then I'll do things on my own, too.

00:15:46.000 --> 00:15:48.010
I'll do this!

00:15:51.070 --> 00:15:55.510
How d'you like that? I've made 
your Nendonaroids super ugly.

00:15:55.730 --> 00:15:59.140
You get it now? You! You! You!

00:16:00.720 --> 00:16:03.050
What am I doing?

00:16:03.050 --> 00:16:05.040
Exactly what I was wondering.

00:16:05.040 --> 00:16:07.090
Instead of pointlessly fleeing from reality,

00:16:07.090 --> 00:16:10.650
if it bothers you, shouldn't you
 go talk with them?

00:16:10.900 --> 00:16:12.780
I told you! I can't ask them that!

00:16:13.200 --> 00:16:14.450
Mile-sama...

00:16:15.060 --> 00:16:20.780
I'm scared. What if Reina-san and the 
others really say they don't need me?

00:16:22.080 --> 00:16:25.710
What if they're out there right now, 
having fun, just the three of them...

00:16:26.180 --> 00:16:27.490
What do I do?

00:16:37.520 --> 00:16:38.970
What are you talking about?

00:16:39.360 --> 00:16:41.350
That will never happen.

00:16:41.750 --> 00:16:43.480
Y-You think so?

00:16:43.650 --> 00:16:44.480
Yes!

00:16:44.480 --> 00:16:48.010
There's no way Reina-dono and the 
others could possibly abandon

00:16:48.010 --> 00:16:49.640
such an unpredictable and comedic character.

00:16:49.640 --> 00:16:51.700
I don't think that's a compliment.

00:16:59.450 --> 00:17:01.580
We're not getting beaten now, 
not after we've come so far!

00:17:01.760 --> 00:17:02.840
Of course not!

00:17:02.840 --> 00:17:06.250
We need to complete this 
quest for the gift budget!

00:17:06.250 --> 00:17:08.080
Wait for us, Mile!

00:17:12.840 --> 00:17:13.970
Guys?

00:17:22.290 --> 00:17:23.220
We did it!

00:17:23.480 --> 00:17:24.230
Yeah!

00:17:25.930 --> 00:17:27.640
Mission complete!

00:17:27.640 --> 00:17:28.610
Guys!

00:17:31.050 --> 00:17:31.900
Mile!

00:17:32.810 --> 00:17:33.360
Th...

00:17:33.960 --> 00:17:35.090
That's so mean!

00:17:35.090 --> 00:17:37.410
How could you go take jobs 
as Hunters without me?

00:17:37.900 --> 00:17:42.040
You're leaving me behind! Just the three 
of you, laughing and giggling...

00:17:42.360 --> 00:17:44.400
Laughing and giggling?

00:17:44.400 --> 00:17:46.400
I-It's not like that, Mile.

00:17:46.400 --> 00:17:47.940
We have reasons for...

00:17:48.750 --> 00:17:51.070
You really don't need me?

00:17:51.070 --> 00:17:53.510
Is this the problem of the rotten mikan?

00:17:53.510 --> 00:17:55.720
Are you firing me and calling it "graduation"?

00:17:55.940 --> 00:17:58.160
I have no idea what you're talking about!

00:17:58.160 --> 00:17:59.640
It's okay, just calm down.

00:17:59.640 --> 00:18:01.350
Mile, behind you! Behind you!

00:18:01.560 --> 00:18:03.600
Is having bigger boobs really so much better?

00:18:03.600 --> 00:18:06.460
Is being flat so wrong?

00:18:09.020 --> 00:18:09.810
Pipe down!

00:18:15.790 --> 00:18:18.030
I trusted you!

00:18:18.030 --> 00:18:21.960
I'm part of the Crimson Vow, too, aren't I?

00:18:23.850 --> 00:18:26.080
Oh dear... She's crying.

00:18:26.310 --> 00:18:30.080
This isn't what I was hoping for.

00:18:35.330 --> 00:18:37.840
Oh, is that what it was?

00:18:38.080 --> 00:18:40.520
You were doing all that for me?

00:18:40.520 --> 00:18:43.430
You should have just said 
so from the beginning.

00:18:43.830 --> 00:18:46.810
If we did that, we wouldn't be 
able to surprise you, would we?

00:18:47.010 --> 00:18:50.600
But since Mile burned that 
cockatrice to a crisp,

00:18:50.600 --> 00:18:52.750
all our work so far went up in smoke.

00:18:52.750 --> 00:18:54.280
It's too bad.

00:18:54.280 --> 00:18:57.570
Just a little more, and we'd have 
been able to buy that accessory.

00:18:57.910 --> 00:19:00.820
Accessory? What are you talking about?

00:19:01.070 --> 00:19:01.830
Huh?

00:19:02.800 --> 00:19:06.050
See? It's that, right? 
The thing you want, Mile.

00:19:06.050 --> 00:19:08.410
That's why we worked so hard to earn money.

00:19:09.160 --> 00:19:11.790
It's quite a costly item.

00:19:11.990 --> 00:19:13.570
Y-You've got it all wrong!

00:19:13.570 --> 00:19:15.720
That's not my taste at all!

00:19:15.720 --> 00:19:17.800
That shiny, ostentatious display of wealth...

00:19:18.060 --> 00:19:19.550
What? Really?

00:19:19.790 --> 00:19:23.050
I think, probably, what I was looking at was...

00:19:23.340 --> 00:19:24.440
Over here!

00:19:25.120 --> 00:19:28.810
What pretty pendants. And 
priced quite reasonably too.

00:19:29.070 --> 00:19:30.010
Right?

00:19:30.010 --> 00:19:33.530
I thought, if it were these, we might 
all be able to get matching ones.

00:19:37.870 --> 00:19:39.100
Mile...

00:19:39.100 --> 00:19:41.820
Honestly, you should have just 
said so from the beginning!

00:19:42.050 --> 00:19:44.000
I'll do that next time.

00:19:46.680 --> 00:19:49.270
These ladies sure like making
things difficult, don't they?

00:19:52.880 --> 00:19:54.210
Now...

00:19:54.600 --> 00:19:59.210
In celebration of the 200th day 
since Mile met the three of us...

00:19:59.610 --> 00:20:00.560
Cheers!

00:20:00.560 --> 00:20:02.050
Cheers!

00:20:06.790 --> 00:20:08.810
Wow! This is pretty lavish.

00:20:08.810 --> 00:20:11.320
We worked hard and went all-out today.

00:20:11.320 --> 00:20:14.770
Don't hold back on the food! 
Eat as much as you want!

00:20:14.770 --> 00:20:17.730
Today's a special anniversary 
for all of you, after all!

00:20:17.730 --> 00:20:19.480
Thank you, Lenny-chan!

00:20:19.820 --> 00:20:21.520
That's right.

00:20:21.940 --> 00:20:24.990
If it's the anniversary of 
Mile meeting us, then...

00:20:24.990 --> 00:20:29.240
It also means it's the anniversary 
of the four of us meeting, right?

00:20:29.240 --> 00:20:31.960
Why are you saying something 
so obvious now, of all times?

00:20:31.960 --> 00:20:35.190
Well, somehow, I didn't realize that.

00:20:35.190 --> 00:20:39.490
I got completely swept up in Reina's fervor 
about throwing a celebration for Mile.

00:20:39.490 --> 00:20:42.260
I got swept up in Reina's fervor, too.

00:20:42.260 --> 00:20:46.310
What are you talking about? 
You guys were excited, too!

00:20:46.310 --> 00:20:47.460
Reina-san!

00:20:47.890 --> 00:20:51.850
This celebration is all 
thanks to you, isn't it?

00:20:52.120 --> 00:20:54.000
I'm so moved!

00:20:54.000 --> 00:20:57.270
Wha? Wait! Mile! Cut that out!

00:20:55.500 --> 00:20:57.270
I'm so happy for you, Reina.

00:20:57.270 --> 00:20:59.800
She's crying with joy, just as you'd hoped.

00:21:00.530 --> 00:21:02.890
Okay! I get it already!

00:21:02.890 --> 00:21:03.740
Honestly...

00:21:05.630 --> 00:21:09.220
But, you know, I was really 
anxious there for a while.

00:21:09.220 --> 00:21:11.530
I thought maybe Reina-san had realized 
I've been measuring her chest

00:21:11.530 --> 00:21:13.000
in the middle of the night.

00:21:13.860 --> 00:21:14.750
What?

00:21:14.750 --> 00:21:19.000
I was so worried that's 
why you all hated me now.

00:21:19.240 --> 00:21:22.800
The way I steal the snacks 
Pauline-san's hidden away...

00:21:23.770 --> 00:21:27.640
Or maybe Mavis-san had found out 
I read her picture diary...

00:21:28.870 --> 00:21:31.760
But I'm so glad it was all 
just a misunderstanding.

00:21:31.760 --> 00:21:35.440
This is what they mean when they 
say "adversity builds character."

00:21:36.150 --> 00:21:39.280
To think that Pauline-san, who immediately 
notices when money goes missing,

00:21:39.280 --> 00:21:42.240
didn't notice cookies going missing.

00:21:42.240 --> 00:21:44.600
It's a weakness I never expected!

00:21:45.680 --> 00:21:48.670
Dad! Mom! Hold the food!

00:21:48.670 --> 00:21:51.700
This is certain to become the 
anniversary of a tragedy.

00:21:52.040 --> 00:21:54.450
What do you mean by that?

00:21:54.700 --> 00:21:57.210
Perhaps you'd like to tell us in detail.

00:21:57.500 --> 00:21:59.960
Tonight looks to be a long night.

00:22:00.250 --> 00:22:00.830
Huh?

00:22:03.210 --> 00:22:05.440
Mile!

00:22:05.440 --> 00:22:08.750
I'm so sorry!

00:22:09.970 --> 00:22:12.890
Didn't I Say to Make My Abilities 
Average in the Next Life?!
